{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1532672-so-how-do-you-stat-mortal-npcs-in-your-game","id":1532672,"title":"So, how do *you* stat mortal NPCs in your game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-15T15:58:50-07:00","id":1532672,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> So, how do *you* stat mortal NPCs in your game?","content":"I've gotten an itch to write, and I'm currently working on a STV supplement called &quot;Bit Parts&quot; that'll include rules for quickly generating minor NPC mortals. I'd like to get an impression on how other Storytellers do theirs.<br /> <br /> The method I'm currently tweaking is meant to be simple enough to fit everything on a 3x5 index card with room left for notes. The barest essentials are that each Bit Player starts with a Competence rating, Notable Attributes (unlisted Attributes are assumed to be 2 dots), and 2-3 fields of Expertise. Competence 1 is typically a bystander out of their depth, Competence 2 or 3 is what I have as &quot;typical,&quot; and Competence 4 is a mortal who shouldn't be underestimated. Whenever they're performing within their Expertise, they use Attribute + Competence. Outside of that, they use Attribute + up to 1/2 Competence (rounded up), as decided by the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> What are your go-to methods when you have to quickly come up with a mortal's stat block? How do you scale their dice pools to fit their intended challenge level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T16:40:38-07:00","id":1532674,"title":"","content":"For me, it depends. If they're a major player I give them a full character sheet, if they're a bit player they get a couple notes and a dice pool or two, if that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T22:13:11-07:00","id":1532682,"title":"","content":"I usually come up with their statistics on the fly. Once I come up with a given statistic, I try to keep it consistent in future scenes. This works for my purposes, likely because I do not have many consequential mortal NPCs in my current game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T01:58:45-07:00","id":1532691,"title":"","content":"I use three methods depending on the point of the NPC:<br /> <br /> No-subsystem NPCs: NPCs that will never be contested using things like full combat or social maneuvering. Any rolling will be one-and-done. I jot down a Resistance traits, and few dice-pools that I think might come up and how competent I want them to be if that happens.<br /> <br /> Minor subsystem NPCs: Character that aren't major narrative focuses of the game, but are going to be involved enough that they need a bit more mechanical heft in case they're expect to be part of conflicts that use the major subsystems of the game. These turn out basically the same as the mortal Antagonists in the CofD corebook in style and length.<br /> <br /> Major NPCs: Full sheets.<br /> <br /> While I would like to switch to something closer to how most Storypath games handle things, it's too much work as too many bits and bobs in the CofD expect both sides of the conflict to at least have their Attributes determined and not just a cluster of most commonly used actions with predetermined final dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T10:51:17-07:00","id":1532705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1532672-so-how-do-you-stat-mortal-npcs-in-your-game?p=1532691#post1532691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor subsystem NPCs: Character that aren't major narrative focuses of the game, but are going to be involved enough that they need a bit more mechanical heft in case they're expect to be part of conflicts that use the major subsystems of the game. These turn out basically the same as the mortal Antagonists in the CofD corebook in style and length.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's about the level I'm working on with Bit Players, maybe just a touch simpler. Aside from Storyteller characters, I also plan on encouraging players to use my subsystem to sketch out the mortals in their lives, including Touchstones, since that's something I have trouble doing myself, sometimes.<br /> <br /> For those who just do ad hoc dice pools, what's the general range you go with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T11:16:13-07:00","id":1532708,"title":"","content":"If I'm winging it: quickly the NPC's &quot;challenge&quot; from 1 to 5 on the physical/social/mental. Anything that requires a static Attribute (Resistance) uses the relevant rating. Dice pools are x2. Modifiers as appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:10:02-07:00","id":1532714,"title":"","content":"If my mortal is a big player in our games and if that is the case and then yes we give them a full write up of there attributes and skills and what kind of role they play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T16:46:54-07:00","id":1532737,"title":"","content":"For ad hoc, generally 3-6. I'm not going to bother rolling a dice pool of 2 most of the time, and if they would have more than 6 dice I probably shouldn't be doing ad hoc with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T19:12:33-07:00","id":1532791,"title":"","content":"Though, in Cyberpunk 2020, we had an NPC-sheet, four to a page, that was nice, but, in CoD, I like to detail all my NPCs to the point they are almost characters, working in a complex-system that is the city or town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}